# __TITLE__

Home Assistant dashboard card. The initial scaffold displays an entity and opens its details; domain-specific controls are added during implementation.

## Install with HACS

[![Open in HACS](https://my.home-assistant.io/badges/hacs_repository.svg)](https://my.home-assistant.io/redirect/hacs_repository/?owner=__OWNER__&repository=__CARD_TAG__&category=plugin)

After the repository is published publicly, add it as a custom Dashboard repository in HACS, download the card and reload the browser. Check the module resource: `/hacsfiles/__CARD_TAG__/__CARD_TAG__.js`.

## Manual installation

Copy `dist/__CARD_TAG__.js` to `/config/www/`. Register `/local/__CARD_TAG__.js?v=0.1.0` as a JavaScript module under Settings > Dashboards > Resources, then reload. On updates replace the file and update the version query on the existing resource.

```yaml
type: custom:__CARD_TAG__
entity: __EXAMPLE_ENTITY__
layout: compact # or wide
```

Choose the entity and layout in the visual editor. An optional name overrides friendly_name. Theme colors, card background, borders and typography use Home Assistant variables.

## Development

```sh
npm install
npm run check
npm run dev
```

Commit the generated package-lock.json and dist bundle. Later installs use npm ci. Open http://127.0.0.1:4173 for the real built card with simulated state. Tests and previews do not prove real-device behavior.

Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) and [the working guide](docs/working-guide.md) for editor, device and release lessons. For an authorized release, synchronize package/lock versions and changelog, rebuild and tag v0.1.0. GitHub workflows test/build, validate HACS for public repos and publish the JavaScript release asset.

